\section{Units in variable names}{

Many internal names end with a suffix that helps identify the value:
\describe{
\item{\verb{_days}}{Days since 1970-01-01 for dates, or elapsed days for
ages and durations. Values may include fractions of a day.}
\item{\verb{_years}}{Time in fractional years, using 365.25 days per year.}
\item{\verb{_ymd}}{A date written as year, month and day without separators,
for example \code{20201103} for 3 November 2020.}
\item{\verb{_idx}}{A state's number in the internal mapping between labels
and numbers.}
\item{\verb{_slot}}{A person's row number in the internal person store.}
\item{\verb{_id}}{A person identifier used in the inputs or output, such as
\code{ID} or \code{motherID}. It need not equal their row number in the store.}
}
